# Previously SHIPPED renders of the match-harness recipe. These are frozen
# artifacts, not source: MATCH_HARNESS_PREVIOUS compares an installed site's
# file against them byte-for-byte (normalize() forgives only CRLF and trailing
# whitespace), so reformatting one would stop matching every site that installed
# that version — the file would be flagged as hand-edited and left broken,
# which is exactly the failure #751's migration exists to repair.
scripts/match-harness-previous/

# Generated analysis data for the meta-week package (machine-written, not source)
docs/meta-week/_data/

# Webflow reference captures (scripts/webflow-capture): the fetched bytes and
# their manifest, kept exactly as the reference served them. Reformatting one
# would change its sha256 and fail check.mjs. CAPTURE.md stays formatted.
captures/*/pages/
captures/*/files/
captures/*/manifest.json

# The seeded-review bake-off's cases: old commits' files and diffs, rebuilt byte
# for byte by build.mjs. Line numbers in key.json point into them, so a
# reformat would move every seeded defect off its range.
scripts/model-bakeoff/tasks/seeded-review/cases/

# The SvelteKit cockpit's generated and build output (#582).
cockpit/.svelte-kit/
cockpit/build/
cockpit/.netlify/
